                                <li>Parts which are subjected to normal wear and tear like seals, filters, brake shoe, belts, rollers, bearings, valves, switches, wheels, tyres, consumables like hydraulic oil, electrolyte etc, and all rubber and electrical items including horns, electric switches, fuses, electric motor brushes, bulbs, spark plugs etc.</li>
                                <li>Any plastic parts affected by discoloration.</li>
                                <li>Any failure due to the external voltage fluctuations.</li>
                                <li>Any damage caused by the failure of any supporting hardware not supplied by NILKAMAL LTD.</li>
                                <li>Parts or components damaged in transit where NILKAMAL is not involved in transportation of goods to purchaser's site. This warranty does not apply to any failure of product due to alterations, modifications, misuse, abuse, neglect, accident, improper maintenance ordo installation, use of parts not supplied by NILKAMAL LTD, failure to operate and use the product in accordance with the instructions provided in the operation's Manual supplied with the product or failure to otherwise meet manufacturer's specifications, or if the serial number has been removed, altered or defaced.</li>
                            </ol>
                        </li>
                        <li><strong>PROCEDURE FOR REQUESTING WARRANTY:</strong> In the event of a problem covered under standard warranty policy, the customer must first contact NILKAMAL LTD through a written email (<a href="mailto:mhe.services@nlikamal.com">services@nlikamal.com</a>)</li>
                        <li><strong>RIGHT TO MODIFY:</strong> NILKAMAL LTD. reserves the right to make changes or improvements in its products without any notice or obligations.</li>
